  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03632v2</id>
    <title>Regularity of the stationary density for systems with fast random switching</title>
    <updated>2023-02-12T12:14:16Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03632v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2212.03632v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We consider the piecewise-deterministic Markov process obtained by randomly switching between the flows generated by a finite set of smooth vector fields on a compact set. We obtain Hörmander-type conditions on the vector fields guaranteeing that the stationary density is: $C^k$ whenever the jump rates are sufficiently fast, for any $k&lt;\infty$; unbounded whenever the jump rates are sufficiently slow and lower semi-continuous regardless of the jump rates. Our proofs are probabilistic, relying on a novel application of stopping times.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math.AP" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
